; shl_amount_at_or_above_word_size: a shift count of 64 or more is out of
; range on both implementations.
;
; Rust guards the amount with `(0..64)` before shifting. Python computes in
; unbounded integers, so before this vector `PUSH 1 / PUSH 64 / SHL` reached
; the push check and raised ARITHMETIC_OVERFLOW instead -- a fault-identity
; divergence -- while `PUSH 0 / PUSH 100 / SHL` completed and pushed 0, a
; fault-versus-success divergence on a verifier-clean four-instruction
; program. Both are admissible to a stored program, so both were reachable
; from a signed account.

PUSH 1
PUSH 64
SHL
HALT
